  "structure": {
    "block_count": 48,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Why Pregnancy Leg Cramps Happen and How to Prevent Them",
        "text_sha256": "369383f80afe73fb88d590cddc58256bbfb498d6cbc0a50f91c7b5b7d1cd1d3d",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Light copy updates, updates to sources, and fact-checked for accuracy.",
        "text_sha256": "03ab6ec71ffcc7c2416587f4ad58dc4805f0a11bd13223d387ea9b28fc87f850",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "leg cramps",
        "text_sha256": "6abdfdc707ab2ca251ceb7452cbec1cf03ae2251b6283b8481b4a3c85f665c52",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You're most likely to get leg cramps during pregnancy when you're lying down — but these painful spasms can stand between you and a good night's sleep.",
        "text_sha256": "0cd4f8933e62a013fbb23e7b97681f669b009716cdfd67bda08c946491d18525",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You're probably already having a hard enough time catching Zzzs these days, with your belly getting bigger by the day and your mind on overdrive — and leg cramps aren't helping.",
        "text_sha256": "e0b1d1e2d1f09ee88639cb1032ff0167fd3b4a7f6c2ca33b81b43fe9b51d7aed",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I’ve been getting charley horses and spasms in my right calf every night when I go to bed, like clockwork!\" says What to Expect Community mom hmj8893.",
        "text_sha256": "912e4fa4eb7a33c26035fe53e9bdc094d873b7e70efe269f597d22a8b61b1333",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I started having leg cramps towards the end of my second trimester,\" adds Community mom lifesadance22.",
        "text_sha256": "283423d6a6b98d83ad80761e05dc06a8bdf1695478b8e731caedaba2103605e6",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Here's what causes leg cramps during pregnancy, plus what you can do to ease them.",
        "text_sha256": "e1c9a93f7ce3b7daf5061420344a0b959647a9497dae02f2e0d35fecdfc20859",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Key Takeaways",
        "text_sha256": "cc3f7f0f4513969e418b56fb93ec0876fd96dd6498395b04301f70dbddff8a45",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pregnancy leg cramps are common and usually start in the second or third trimester, often at night. They may be linked to fatigue, circulation changes, mineral imbalances, and pregnancy hormones.",
        "text_sha256": "49b75c9b604d317128ed9e38fc54b4a73b229e6743993cdb906d00d014a3e108",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "For fast relief from leg cramps, try to straighten and flex your foot toward your shin, stand or walk, use cold first (then heat if needed), and consider gentle massage.",
        "text_sha256": "a3689a305175820ea76bcbab8a4d5afcae77a576fc6e2266e147fbba336f1bfd",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "You may be able to reduce the frequency of leg cramps by stretching before bed, staying hydrated, eating enough calcium and magnesium, wearing compression socks, and taking your prenatal vitamin.",
        "text_sha256": "1d9fab9d26ba0813fca15dbf1f70f93a66fa8d4781880cbf7a31d80c209be4ce",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Call your practitioner if the pain is severe, persistent, or comes with swelling or redness.",
        "text_sha256": "b62f0201d9e46fb35b25f979d982bbc378ca27521a925a6fe55ef01b43ffa06f",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "When do leg cramps start during pregnancy?",
        "text_sha256": "18d7d4e4932c56619cba61862256e924831922237a1ff31faa78279f1b0547f1",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Also sometimes called \"charley horses,\" leg cramps during pregnancy usually start in the second or third trimester.",
        "text_sha256": "07d150233edeacb64ac1d1e886be45991f69877afb59442e078a928b1f04feb1",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "These painful spasms that radiate through the calves and up the legs are very common among the expectant set. Although they can be felt during the day, they're usually more noticeable at night, when fatigue and fluid accumulation are at their peak (and when you have all that quiet and stillness to ponder them). Trusted SourceKidsHealth From NemoursHow Can I Relieve My Pregnancy Leg Cramps?See All Sources [1]",
        "text_sha256": "3738ac25b4935635047d76b8acf0e2a59019dec8f0ec4b37ae3777d0a6ed34f4",
        "word_count": 68
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceKidsHealth From NemoursHow Can I Relieve My Pregnancy Leg Cramps?See All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "569f23e242c7323069d89d39f6980385c329e5bdbfb5849a2902074791eccb9f",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Leg cramps at midnight? Heartburn at 3 a.m.? The What to Expect app makes it easy to track every ache, twitch, and twinge — so you can spot patterns, share symptoms with your doctor, and get support when you need it most.",
        "text_sha256": "0a57e9052296468ad81e064ee21d1bb8936c727116f8b193f167143529dad0ee",
        "word_count": 42
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What causes leg cramps during pregnancy?",
        "text_sha256": "00cd65364dfbba2336fc8a15bb62455c9a725eb5759465d1b3311e9377fe030d",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Short answer: Nobody's quite sure. Various theories point to the following causes of leg cramps during pregnancy: Trusted SourceMayo ClinicWhat causes leg cramps during pregnancy, and can they be prevented?See All Sources [2]",
        "text_sha256": "719acc8ace17817398f55d390ef40e120afa4a91973ef38073364a5f4d0ba9de",
        "word_count": 33
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceMayo ClinicWhat causes leg cramps during pregnancy, and can they be prevented?See All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "a8888d7e74e97aebae8ff9bf45e6bd72af6a6f5945b1595b594b27b6b6e6b2a0",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pregnancy fatigue from carrying the extra baby weight",
        "text_sha256": "16b0753bf48d64f1926f05ed6187d39a48d356770557da1da53686909f6d026b",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Compression of the blood vessels in the legs",
        "text_sha256": "beeba9374243689f289d88b8a99f5eb006d38aaced1dcdc3e99607fde04897c7",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Diet (an excess of phosphorus and a shortage of calcium or magnesium)",
        "text_sha256": "78cab5dfa64577ee3b186189a255efd7dec6b3bd807efcc3119846815cae8283",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pregnancy hormones, since they're often the scapegoat for many pregnancy aches and pains",
        "text_sha256": "1d5b395e59c8ac877b74d42b37422e9c74667bfca97e00e2b29a77e8ffdeb407",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "How can I get rid of leg cramps when I’m pregnant?",
        "text_sha256": "d2ae96ef78c2e6f805ab23291dc7a4a4e084c91bba78d7e8d1499f86b1321c7c",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "When you get a leg cramp, try the following:",
        "text_sha256": "a4bced7960367278f4c91bb66f633ccaa68f43a4159afff4771e324724590c5f",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Flex your feet. Straighten your leg and gently flex your ankle and toes back toward your shins several times. You can do this in bed, but you may find you get faster relief if you get up and do it on your feet.",
        "text_sha256": "3ff251417fa928bec1ab158b067fc7c85572de5c56815f9b542478969972d6b9",
        "word_count": 43
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Cool it. Try standing on a cold surface, which can sometimes stop a spasm. An ice pack or cool compress may also help.",
        "text_sha256": "c69340cc7609744268f015eaaecd5a74a5c4f45653a487224d1dc4b33cfb3c33",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Warm up. If stretching and cold help subside the pain, try a heating pad for added relief. (Don’t use heat if pain persists.)",
        "text_sha256": "a1ba6f3fde693165a695666da9202f84b3a87490d6047b29100d612086991648",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Get a massage. Treat yourself to a prenatal massage , or ask your partner to give you a rub-down. (Don't massage if pain persists.)",
        "text_sha256": "62dd4e1a8638195c328f3bc8e75587557403e2b4648be755375fdb0a76f156ef",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000031",
        "block_index": 31,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Can I prevent leg cramps during pregnancy?",
        "text_sha256": "27f64beeb64b142ad5b9a0fe90ae75e9403d2f2707a3460270872621483e69ba",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000032",
        "block_index": 32,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "While leg cramps during pregnancy aren't exactly preventable, there are a few steps you can take to minimize the frequency and duration:",
        "text_sha256": "ae562c3fe7ad3d9f6e43e9d369427938c454cda583cf158aaa57b606f5f56c5b",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000033",
        "block_index": 33,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Try stretching exercises. Stop cramps before they strike with a few pregnancy-safe stretching exercises . Before you head to bed, stand about 2 feet away from a wall and put your palms flat against it. Lean forward, keeping your heels on the floor. Hold the stretch for 10 seconds, then relax for five. Try this three times. Trusted SourceMayo ClinicOffice StretchesSee All Sources [3]",
        "text_sha256": "8d439a8e3c6d14050104d8569d8ad5821acf7667d2b8f6fbd433ed3bef6f197a",
        "word_count": 64
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000034",
        "block_index": 34,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Switch it up. Alternate periods of activity with periods of rest throughout the day.",
        "text_sha256": "dd63cfd9722d606a7aa089b24f047aa14b3cd989fda150b2807371955b479cb7",
        "word_count": 14
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000035",
        "block_index": 35,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Put your feet up. Kick back with your feet raised as often as you can when you're seated.",
        "text_sha256": "0f75326ca5dfd544171fd7b4dba535f6c5d37047770ea98e69f903ea3210a318",
        "word_count": 18
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000036",
        "block_index": 36,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Update your wardrobe. Try sporting a pair of compression socks during the day, which may help reduce swelling in the ankles and feet by improving circulation in your lower extremities. If possible, try to wear shoes with a firm heel counter (the part that cups the heel) to properly position your foot in the shoe. Trusted SourceNational Library of Medicine, Medline PlusCompression StockingsSee All Sources [4]",
        "text_sha256": "e783077a7099f75cb6a7ada31237fa609bd84b700d29bedc4179d3f64c1b1872",
        "word_count": 66
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000037",
        "block_index": 37,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Stay hydrated . Make sure you're drinking plenty of water (most pregnant women need about eight to 10 glasses of fluids a day, but ask your practitioner if you need more). A good sign you’re hydrated: Your pee is light yellow, not straw-colored.",
        "text_sha256": "7fc327770d15a51b0f4b86cffeb517141c7e232223f3d1bb58798e5550e32a22",
        "word_count": 43
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000038",
        "block_index": 38,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Eat a well-balanced diet . It should include lots of calcium (try yogurt, which may also help with pregnancy constipation ) and magnesium (bananas are full of it).",
        "text_sha256": "1feec90daaad18719baa2ad55127958a607b623f52b8fd4c83d5e6ce9dde4795",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000039",
        "block_index": 39,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Take your prenatal vitamin every day. This can help ensure you're getting all the vitamins and minerals you and baby need while you're pregnant.",
        "text_sha256": "50bf2ee6adc0cde46e7440523fb57b5f8cf3b9842100c3e6a5dfc3acfb6d7cd8",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000040",
        "block_index": 40,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Talk to your practitioner. Ask if you should be taking a magnesium supplement before going to bed.",
        "text_sha256": "f2e1671bb6daa05d318711c282932fefb40dd191371c470fc587c18858486382",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000041",
        "block_index": 41,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Try a glass of milk with a banana before bed. Some patients report that this magnesium-rich combo aids relaxation, which in turn may help you fall asleep.",
        "text_sha256": "bc0bc36becbb779558222633dbdffd62019acabe25516230b65357b473008141",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000042",
        "block_index": 42,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "When can I expect leg cramps to end while I'm pregnant?",
        "text_sha256": "d6f58794a96a78ec717b3907eab7bbbef563853f628446a51b0cc277f96f4a85",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000043",
        "block_index": 43,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Really bad cramps (like a charley horse) can cause pain for a few days, and that's nothing to worry about.",
        "text_sha256": "713e29f5b44fc5aeaa8690a8af6f63bf8b9d56a674d9aacf0b98f588d3cf55b0",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000044",
        "block_index": 44,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Leg cramps are especially common in the second half of pregnancy, when pregnancy weight gain , increased swelling, and overall fatigue are at their high points — and interruptions to your sleep are most frustrating.",
        "text_sha256": "faacfe3553d5d2cae0d89e4e8b33672c81d59dc0947d5ececec380df75424718",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000045",
        "block_index": 45,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Unfortunately for most women, leg cramps last through the third trimester of pregnancy . Taking steps to reduce leg cramps (drinking lots of water, eating a well-balanced diet, stretching) can help keep them at bay.",
        "text_sha256": "06284c172eee6ae66caf1b5cdafa66f2e844d9c73f4e5c2e959c2df57b232709",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000046",
        "block_index": 46,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "When to see your doctor about leg cramps",
        "text_sha256": "0ba289ac5bdecade395fbcb1486d00750606c8f6688e9c1f2d841f38ac12cda5",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000047",
        "block_index": 47,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If the pain is severe and persistent, and if you notice swelling, warmth or redness in the area, talk to your practitioner. In very rare cases you could have a blood clot in a vein known as deep vein thrombosis (DVT) that requires medical attention.",
        "text_sha256": "a6aaac0938a0c0fc7a25f23b86837b5cac4c9020845be323c38c0bba055e4fd2",
        "word_count": 45
      }
    ],
    "content_word_count": 1104,
    "heading_count": 8
  },
  "title": "Why Pregnancy Leg Cramps Happen and How to Prevent Them",
